## The best line {notes="notes/week2_notes.md#best-line"}

::: {.columns}
::: {.column width="55%"}

::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![](week2_files/figure-revealjs/residuals-1.png){width=1050}
:::
:::

:::

::: {.column width="45%"}
- The [red lines]{.red} are the **misses**: how far each person is from the line.
- The best line makes the misses as small as possible overall.
- [With standardized data and one predictor, the best β is exactly the correlation:
  **β = r = 0.75**.]{.fragment}
:::
:::

## Reading the coefficient {.mechanics notes="notes/week2_notes.md#reading-coef"}


::: {.cell}

:::


::: {.columns}
::: {.column width="45%"}
- In z-scores: **β = 0.75**
  - "An adult 1 SD taller than average is, on average, 0.75 SD heavier."
- Back in real units: β × SD~weight~ / SD~height~
  - 0.75 × 6.5 / 7.7 = **0.63 kg per cm**
  - "Each extra centimeter of height goes with about 0.63 kg more
    weight."
:::

::: {.column width="55%"}

::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![](week2_files/figure-revealjs/slope-plot-1.png){width=1050}
:::
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
coef(lm(weight ~ height, data = howell))
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
(Intercept)      height 
 -52.316178    0.629421 
```


:::
:::

:::
:::

